# Split Constants and Utils

When implementing a feature, updating behavior, or fixing a bug, extract reusable static values and pure helpers out of components, hooks, and stores. Keep UI/orchestration thin.

## Placement

| Kind | Put in | Examples |
|------|--------|----------|
| Static values | `features/<feature>/constants/` | Copy strings, labels, phase/status enums, magic numbers, fixed sets/maps |
| Pure helpers | `features/<feature>/utils/` | Mappers, resolvers, formatters, validators, correlation keys, message builders |

Reuse the feature’s existing `constants/` and `utils/` folders (and barrel `index.ts` exports) when present. Do not invent a parallel structure.

## Rules

- Do **not** hardcode user-facing copy, phase names, or status literals inside components/hooks when they can live in `constants/`.
- Do **not** leave reusable mapping / phase / validation logic inline in JSX or large components when it belongs in `utils/`.
- Prefer pure, named exports: `export const FOO = … as const` and `export const resolveBar = (…) => …`.
- Import from feature barrels when they exist (`@/features/<feature>/constants`, `@/features/<feature>/utils`).
- Skip extraction only for one-off values used in a single place with no reuse and no clarity gain.

## Examples

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — copy and phase logic buried in the component
if (status === "rejected") return <h2>Cancelled by you</h2>;

// ✅ GOOD — constants + util
// features/booking/constants/confirm-booking-copy.ts
export const CONFIRM_BOOKING = {
  rejectedTitle: "Cancelled by you",
} as const;

// features/booking/utils/create-booking-card-phase.ts
export const resolveCreateHitlCardPhase = ({ decisionStatus, … }) => { … };
```

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — magic strings scattered across files
outcome?.phase === "success"

// ✅ GOOD — shared constant
outcome?.phase === CREATE_BOOKING_CARD_PHASE.SUCCESS
```

## Checklist (before finishing the change)

- [ ] New/changed copy and enums live under `constants/`
- [ ] New/changed pure helpers live under `utils/`
- [ ] Components/hooks orchestrate; they do not own reusable data or pure logic
- [ ] Existing constants/utils reused before adding duplicates
